<newsitem itemid="633302" id="root" date="1997-06-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Caxton ups year share, dividend.</title>
<headline>Caxton ups year share, dividend.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		     184.9	 vs 170.5</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)		22.0	  vs 18.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income		  50.83	 vs 43.55</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  144.08	vs 126.07</p>
<p>    Tax				46.19	 vs 42.48</p>
<p>    Interest &amp; finance charges 0.29	  vs 8.08</p>
<p>    Turnover			 1,119.17    vs 965.07</p>
<p>Div payable July 25</p>
<p>on register June 27</p>
<p>Full name: Caxton Limited</p>
<p>Note - The company said underutilisation of increased capacity in certain divisions namely book publishing, printing, web printing, together with increased competition led to a drop in operating margins. It said earnings per share were diluted by the increased number of shares in issue.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
